course: dictionary
lesson: 10862
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. The word vice is a good example.
explain: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» The clue is virtues. Virtues are good, so vices must be the opposite: bad habits.
explain: When you meet vice, ask what kind of sentence it is in. Is it about behaviour, a tool, or a person's job? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A vice is a bad habit or a wrong way of behaving.
fact: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» Virtues are the opposite of vices.
fact: Vice can also mean a serious crime, such as illegal gambling.
fact: In British English, a vice is a tool with two jaws that holds something firmly while you work on it. Americans spell it «vise».
fact: The prefix vice- means next in rank below the top person, as in vice-captain.
exercise: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» What is a vice? | A type of food | A kind of animal | A good habit, like honesty | *A bad habit, such as greed
exercise: Your teacher says, «Clamp the wood in the vice before you saw it.» What is a vice in this sentence? | A kind of bird | *A tool with two jaws that holds things firmly | The head teacher | A bad habit
exercise: Ella is the vice-captain of the netball team. What does vice- tell you? | The captain of another team | The captain's enemy | *Next in rank below the captain | A captain who cheats
test:
Which of these is a vice, according to «vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty»? | Honesty | Courage | *Cruelty | Kindness
A school has a principal and a vice-principal. What does vice-principal mean? | *Second in charge, below the principal | The person who cleans the school | The principal's best friend | A new school built next door
exam:
Which sentence uses vice as a tool? | *Dad tightened the wood in the vice before he started sawing. | Greed is a vice that makes people unkind. | Ella is the vice-captain of the netball team. | Good habits are called virtues.
